## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical understanding of online ICA workflow for mobile, real-time audio with nonstationary noise.

## Key Concepts
- Online whitening and demixing; frame-wise updating; permutation alignment.
- Handling nonstationarity; simple energy/phase cues for gating frames.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: simple whitening placeholder (not a full ICA)
function whiten(X) {
  // X: [frames, channels]
  const M = covariance(X);
  const {eigvec, eigval} = eigenDecomp(M);
  return X.dot(eigvec).div(sqrt(eigval));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this to 4 microphones with more moving sources?
- What metrics besides SDR/SIR would help validate perceptual quality?

Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical, time-domain ICA approach for a minimal two-channel setup, avoiding frequency-domain tricks and focusing on core steps and risks.

Key Concepts
- Centering and whitening of 2-channel data
- ICA algorithm choice (FastICA vs JADE) for a small system
- Handling permutation and sign indeterminacy
- Convergence criteria and stopping rules
- Evaluation with SDR/SIR and ground-truth strategies

Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for a 2-channel ICA pipeline
function twoChannelICA(X) {
  // X: 2 x N data
  let Xc = center(X);
  let [V,D] = eig(Xc.kCov());
  let Xw = V * diag(1./sqrt(D)) * V^T * Xc;
  let W = FastICA2x2(Xw);
  let S = W * Xw;
  return S;
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to 3 sources with 2 channels?
- What failure modes dominate in short recordings or highly nonstationary noises?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess practical blind source separation pipeline design under real-time, network-induced constraints for collaboration tools deployed at scale.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming BSS with time-varying mixing matrices
- Synchronization strategies for asynchronous inputs and packet loss
- Joint diagonalization versus per-bin ICA trade-offs
- Latency budgeting and robustness to network jitter
- Evaluation methodology using SDR/SIR metrics plus perceptual validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: online BSS for 2 sources, 4 mics
function onlineBSS(micFrames) {
  // Synchronize misaligned frames
  const syncedFrames = synchronizeStreams(micFrames);

  // STFT processing
  const stftFrames = syncedFrames.map(frame => stft(frame));

  // Estimate time-varying mixing matrix
  const mixingMatrix = estimateMixingMatrix(stftFrames);

  // Apply spatially varying whitening
  const whitened = spatialWhitening(stftFrames, mixingMatrix);

  // Joint diagonalization for source separation
  const separatedSources = jointDiagonalization(whitened);

  return separatedSources;
}
```

